<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamzat Bek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1789–1834</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamzat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">Bek</a> was the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of the Caucasian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a>, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-muhammad">Ghazi Muhammad</a> after his death at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gimry">Gimry</a> in 1832. In 1834 he took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khunzakh">Khunzakh</a> and massacred the family of the Avar khans. Weeks later he was assassinated in a mosque by Avar kinsmen, including Hadji Murad, and Shamil became imam.</p></div>
